## Results
### Primary outcome
Transfusion occurred in 12% of the tranexamic acid group and 31% of the placebo group (RR 0.39, 95% CI 0.24–0.62).
### Secondary outcomes
Major bleeding requiring intervention: see Table 1.
- No thromboembolic events in either group.
- Length of stay did not differ.
Figure 1. Flow of participants through the trial.

## Methods
We randomized 240 adults aged ≥18 y to tranexamic acid or placebo.
### Outcomes
The primary outcome was transfusion; secondary outcomes included major bleeding (P < 0.05 for significance).
### Statistical analysis
Risk ratios were computed as with 95% CI.

## Introduction
Bleeding after hip surgery is common.

## Discussion
Tranexamic acid reduced transfusion & major bleeding.

